WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.409
This fictional pilot brief authorizes one week of practice on fictional intake cases.

00:00:05.409 --> 00:00:07.906
Put that limited fact under Confirmed.

00:00:07.906 --> 00:00:13.731
A draft may help organize the first summary, but no saving has been measured.

00:00:13.731 --> 00:00:19.140
Put the possible benefit under Expected and say what the pilot will examine.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.804
Wider use remains undecided.

00:00:20.804 --> 00:00:22.884
Put that question under Open.

00:00:22.884 --> 00:00:30.374
The service reviewer checks every draft, and the service manager reviews the practice log before a continue-or-stop decision.

00:00:30.374 --> 00:00:33.286
Put those assigned human duties under Responsible.

00:00:33.286 --> 00:00:37.863
Do not promote a simulated listening concern into actual staff feedback.

00:00:37.863 --> 00:00:42.856
In your project, use approved sources and retain the actual checking date.

00:00:42.856 --> 00:00:46.601
If pilot approval has not been supplied, say proposed.

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:52.010
The four headings help the reader understand both the evidence and its limits.
